<!--
  Hand-built against the CMI CDWS response shape, NOT captured. See
  tests/fixtures/README.md.

  The **structure** is measured: run 22 (2026-08-05) read the live
  canton_zurich MITGLIEDER index and section B printed its 55 columns, so the
  nesting here is the real one. That matters, because the first version of this
  file had it wrong: it put the person's fields at the top level, copied from
  `goifer`'s *normalised* output, when the service nests them under
  Person/Kontakt. The probe's field names were wrong the same way and the live
  run reported "3,862 rows with no name" — which reads as a fact about the
  source and was a fact about the probe.

  The **people are invented** and hold no seat anywhere. So are the values of
  every contact field.

  Three things this fixture deliberately encodes, because the probe's answers
  turn on them:

  - a record carries TWO GUIDs. Anna Muster has two rows — one Kantonsrat seat,
    one commission — with two different `OBJ_GUID`s and ONE
    `Person/Kontakt/@OBJ_GUID`, which is what makes the row key a row and the
    person key a person.
  - `Geburtsjahr` is a birth *year*, not a date. That is what the live index
    returns, and a year-precision value is a different claim from P569.
  - NO element carries anything resembling a Staatsarchiv member id. That is
    not an assertion about the live service — run 22's section C crashed before
    it could ask — it is the shape the parsing tests need.
-->
